    "diff_hunk": "@@ -1481,6 +1481,57 @@ these steps:\n [[HR-TIME-3#sec-tools]] when creating these and exchanging them with JavaScript. [[HR-TIME]]\n \n \n+<h3 id=singleton>Singletons</h3>\n+\n+The following types can be used as inputs or outputs of algorithmic prose to improve comprehension.\n+They have no web-visible representation beyond their effect on the flow of any given algorithm, and\n+they can only be compared with \"is\".\n+\n+<dl>\n+ <dt><dfn export>allowed</dfn>\n+ <dd><p>Indicates that some operation is permitted, often used in opposition to <a>blocked</a>.\n+\n+ <dt><dfn export>blocked</dfn>\n+ <dd><p>Indicates that some operation is not permitted, often used in opposition to\n+ <a>allowed</a>.\n+\n+ <dt><dfn export>failure</dfn>\n+ <dd><p>Indicates that some operation did not proceed as expected, often used in opposition to\n+ <a>success</a> or in combination with a more concrete type.\n+\n+ <dt><dfn export>success</dfn>\n+ <dd><p>Indicates that some operation proceeded as expected, often used in opposition to\n+ <a>failure</a>.\n+</dl>\n+\n+<div class=example id=example-singleton-return-and-comparison>\n+ <p>The following algorithm returns <a>success</a> or <a>failure</a>:\n+\n+ <ol>\n+  <li><p>If something unexpectedly bad happened, then return <a>failure</a>.\n+  <li><p>Return <a>success</a>.\n+ </ol>\n+\n+ <p>Callers of that algorithm might evaluate the result as follows:\n+\n+ <ol>\n+  <li><p>If <var>result</var> is <a>failure</a>, then shut everything down gracefully and abort.\n+  <li><p><a>Assert</a>: <var>result</var> is <a>success</a>.\n+  <li><p>...\n+ </ol>\n+</div>\n+\n+<div class=example id=example-singleton-failure>\n+ <p><a>Failure</a> is often used as the result of an algorithm that can fail or return a value:\n+\n+ <ol>\n+  <li><p>If <var>status</var> is less than 200 or greater than 599, then return <a>failure</a>.\n+\n+  <li><p>Return <var>status</var>.",
